Keep the EGL window surface bottom-left on OHOS.

ANGLE's Vulkan backend reports EGL_SURFACE_ORIENTATION_INVERT_Y_ANGLE as
the optimal orientation, so NativeViewGLSurfaceEGL created a top-left
surface. Drawing to it was right, but copies out of it were upside down:
backdrop-filter and the touch selection magnifier, which read their
backdrop from the framebuffer, showed the page mirrored about the middle
of the screen (the magnifier showed the blank area at the bottom as an
opaque capsule). On OHOS the surface keeps the usual bottom-left origin and
ANGLE flips it when presenting.

It also carries the OHOS copy of Android's PowerVR ASTC rule (id 971 in
gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json) up to Chromium 154.0.8037.97, which
renamed reset_base_level_for_astc_sub_image to reset_base_level_for_astc_image;
the old name failed gpu/config/process_json.py. The main patch, which adds
the rule, has the new version for fresh trees.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-egl-bottom-left-surface.patch

diff --git a/ui/gl/gl_surface_egl.cc b/ui/gl/gl_surface_egl.cc
index 6f03a4e..e32a267 100644
--- a/ui/gl/gl_surface_egl.cc
+++ b/ui/gl/gl_surface_egl.cc
@@ -388,6 +388,12 @@ bool NativeViewGLSurfaceEGL::Initialize(GLSurfaceFormat format) {
     egl_window_attributes.push_back(EGL_TRUE);
   }
 
+  // OHOS: ANGLE's Vulkan backend asks for an inverted-Y window surface, but
+  // a copy out of that surface -- what backdrop-filter and the touch
+  // magnifier read their backdrop from -- came out upside down: the backdrop
+  // showed the page mirrored about the middle of the screen. Keep the usual
+  // bottom-left surface; ANGLE flips it when presenting.
+#if !BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
   if (display_->ext->b_EGL_ANGLE_surface_orientation) {
     EGLint attrib;
     eglGetConfigAttrib(display_->GetDisplay(), GetConfig(),
@@ -396,6 +402,7 @@ bool NativeViewGLSurfaceEGL::Initialize(GLSurfaceFormat format) {
                           ? gfx::SurfaceOrigin::kTopLeft
                           : gfx::SurfaceOrigin::kBottomLeft;
   }
+#endif
 
   if (surface_origin_ == gfx::SurfaceOrigin::kTopLeft) {
     egl_window_attributes.push_back(EGL_SURFACE_ORIENTATION_ANGLE);
